{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Cross-repo VD-2 contract: relay action payloads built by the REAL SSP Wallet builders (src/lib/vaultRelayPayload.ts) from the shared vd-vectors.json, and the rejection payloads SSP Key posts back. SSP Wallet asserts its builders reproduce `payload` byte for byte; SSP Key asserts it parses, routes and verifies every `payload` (and produces every rejection `payload`). Identical copies: ~/repos/sec-2026-10/vd-relay-payloads.json, ssp-wallet tests/lib/fixtures/, ssp-key tests/lib/fixtures/.",
  "regenerate": "Only when the wire format changes on purpose: rebuild with the wallet builders, then copy the file to all three locations.",
  "transport": {
    "vaultDescriptor": "JSON object nested inside the JSON-string payload (never a JSON string of its own), exactly as SSP Enterprise sent it.",
    "vaultDescriptorHash": "64 lowercase hex characters, verbatim.",
    "rejectionCode": "SSP Key puts the machine-readable refusal in `errorCode` (VAULT_DESCRIPTOR_CHANGED | VAULT_DESCRIPTOR_MISSING | VAULT_DESCRIPTOR_INVALID | VAULT_PIN_REFUSED). SSP Wallet reads `errorCode` (and, defensively, `code`) and returns it to SSP Enterprise; any other refusal is KEY_REJECTED.",
    "changeRule": "Honest builder change goes back to the input (source) address, or vault address 0. SSP Key treats only those as change and SHOWS every other output, including other addresses of the same vault, as a recipient. SSP Wallet labels any output paying vault address 0..19 as change and shows it in its change list with the address index. Both accept honest change; neither hides an output."
  },
